  "notes": "ファン is from English \"fan\" and refers to an enthusiastic supporter or admirer of a person, team, or activity.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜のファン: a fan of ~\n- ファンレター: fan letter\n- ファンクラブ: fan club\n- {熱狂的|ねっきょうてき}なファン: passionate/devoted fan\n- {俄|にわか}ファン: bandwagon fan, fair-weather fan\n- ファン{層|そう}: fan base\n\nHOMONYM:\nThe same word ファン also means a mechanical fan or ventilator ({換気|かんき}ファン = ventilation fan). Context makes the meaning clear.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- サポーター: supporter (especially for sports teams)\n- マニア: enthusiast, geek (deeper obsession with a hobby or topic)\n- オタク: otaku, nerd (strong devotion, often to anime/manga/games)",
